course: dictionary
lesson: 4386
title: Hadrosaurs, the duck-billed dinosaurs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hadrosaur is a kind of dinosaur, and the sentence tells you what it is. «Duck-billed dinosaurs, or hadrosaurs, such as Edmontosaurus had hundreds of teeth packed together to grind plants.» The word "or" is a clue: it tells you that hadrosaurs are another name for duck-billed dinosaurs.
explain: Look at the other words for more clues. "Grind plants" tells you hadrosaurs ate plants, not meat. "Duck-billed" tells you the shape of the mouth, which was wide and flat, like a duck's beak.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit: "The hadrosaur ate ___." Plants fit, and so does "herds" from the science lessons, which tells you they lived in groups. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A hadrosaur is a duck-billed dinosaur: a large plant-eating dinosaur with a wide, flat mouth like a duck's beak.
fact: Hadrosaurs lived in the Late Cretaceous, about 100 to 66 million years ago.
fact: Hadrosaurs lived in North America, Asia and Europe.
fact: Some hadrosaurs, like Parasaurolophus, had a hollow crest on their head that may have made honking sounds.
fact: Hadrosaurs had hundreds of teeth for grinding plants, and they lived in herds.
exercise: «Duck-billed dinosaurs, or hadrosaurs, had hundreds of teeth packed together to grind plants.» What is a hadrosaur? | A flying reptile with a long tail | A small fish from the sea | A hunting dinosaur with sharp claws for meat | *A duck-billed dinosaur that ate plants
exercise: Which dinosaur had a hollow crest on its head that may have made honking sounds? | Tyrannosaurus | *Parasaurolophus | Triceratops | Maiasaura
exercise: In «Duck-billed dinosaurs, or hadrosaurs», what does "or" tell you? | *Hadrosaurs are another name for duck-billed dinosaurs | Hadrosaurs are a type of fish | The hadrosaurs all disappeared | It starts a question
test: What did hadrosaurs eat? | Meat from other dinosaurs | *Plants, which they ground with hundreds of teeth | Insects from the ground | Fish from the rivers
test: Scientists found nests and babies of which hadrosaur in Montana, USA? | Parasaurolophus | *Maiasaura | Tyrannosaurus | Edmontosaurus
exam: When did hadrosaurs live? | About 10,000 years ago | Only in the last thousand years | Only in the last hundred years | *About 100 to 66 million years ago
